<SECTION SCID = "T010037A089S"><SCTITLE/>

<PARA INFOID = "T010037A089" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "20Sep2003"     INFOTYPE = "PARTS" INDSW = "ON">
<TITLE>Fuel General</TITLE>
<LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>A fuel returnless system has been adopted for excellent emission performance.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>Quick connectors have been adopted at each connection of the fuel pipes to improve serviceability.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>A fuel pump integrating parts such as the charcoal canister and fuel filter has been adopted and located inside the fuel tank, reducing the number of parts, reducing weight and saving space in the engine room.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>A fixed-torque type fuel tank cap, which cannot be tightened further once tightened a certain amount, has been adopted. This reduces the operating force of the fuel tank cap, ensuring excellent operability.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>By adopting an air filter at the mouth of the fuel tank inlet pipe, underfloor space has been secured.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<FIGURE>
<GRAPHIC GRAPHICNAME = "a4740012p" WIDTH = "7.917in" HEIGHT = "4.875in" />
</FIGURE>
</PARA>
</SECTION>
<SECTION SCID = "T010037A095S"><SCTITLE/>

<PARA INFOID = "T010037A095" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "20Sep2003"     INFOTYPE = "PARTS" INDSW = "ON">
<TITLE>Fuel Returnless System</TITLE>
<LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>The pressure regulator integrated with the fuel pump returns fuel within the fuel tank, supplying only the amount consumed by the engine at a constant fuel pressure. As a result, fuel heated while passing through the engine room does not return to the fuel tank, suppressing the generation of evaporative gas in the fuel tank for excellent emission performance.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<FIGURE>
<GRAPHIC GRAPHICNAME = "a4740013p" WIDTH = "6.903in" HEIGHT = "2.750in" />
</FIGURE>
</PARA>
</SECTION>
<SECTION SCID = "T010037A094S"><SCTITLE/>

<PARA INFOID = "T010037A094" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "20Sep2003"     INFOTYPE = "PARTS" INDSW = "ON">
<TITLE>Fuel tank</TITLE>
<LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>A fuel tank with a capacity of 60L has been installed under the floor of the first and second seats, achieving a spacious interior.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>The material is aluminum-plated steel sheet, and the use of lead has been eliminated in consideration of environmental impact.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>A fuel drain mark has been provided on the bottom surface of the fuel tank to clarify and simplify positioning of the fuel draining device during dismantling and to ensure reliable fuel draining.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>By adopting an aluminum heat insulator, fuel temperature rise has been suppressed and weight has been reduced.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<FIGURE>
<GRAPHIC GRAPHICNAME = "a4740014p" WIDTH = "6.903in" HEIGHT = "5.625in" />
</FIGURE>
<SPEC ID = "T010037A094X01" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>Fuel Tank Specifications (Common to 2WD and 4WD)</TITLE>
<TABLE FRAME = "ALL" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1">
<TGROUP COLS = "2" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1" TGROUPSTYLE = "Table_01">
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "1" COLNAME = "1" COLWIDTH = "49%"/>
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "2" COLNAME = "2" COLWIDTH = "49%"/>
<TBODY>
<ROW ROWSEP = "0">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>Capacity [L]</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2" ALIGN = "CENTER"><PTXT>60</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
</TBODY>
</TGROUP></TABLE></SPEC>
</PARA>
</SECTION>
<SECTION SCID = "T010037A090S"><SCTITLE/>

<PARA INFOID = "T010054A090" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "20Sep2003"     INFOTYPE = "PARTS" INDSW = "ON">
<TITLE>Fuel Pump</TITLE>
<LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>A circumferential flow type in-tank fuel pump has been adopted.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>By integrating the charcoal canister, fuel filter and pressure regulator into the fuel pump assembly, the number of parts and weight have been reduced and space in the engine room has been saved.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<FIGURE>
<GRAPHIC GRAPHICNAME = "a4740015p" WIDTH = "6.903in" HEIGHT = "2.819in" />
</FIGURE>
<SPEC ID = "T010054A090X01" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>Fuel Pump Specifications</TITLE>
<TABLE FRAME = "ALL" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1">
<TGROUP COLS = "2" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1" TGROUPSTYLE = "Table_01">
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "1" COLNAME = "1" COLWIDTH = "49%"/>
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "2" COLNAME = "2" COLWIDTH = "49%"/>
<TBODY>
