</ROW>
</TBODY>
</TGROUP></TABLE></SPEC>
</PARA>
</SECTION>
<SECTION SCID = "T010037A092S"><SCTITLE/>

<PARA INFOID = "T010037A092" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "20Sep2003"     INFOTYPE = "PARTS" INDSW = "ON">
<TITLE>Fuel Delivery Pipe</TITLE>
<LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>An aluminum alloy fuel delivery pipe has been adopted.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>A pulsation damper has been provided in the fuel delivery pipe to reduce fuel pulsation.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<FIGURE>
<GRAPHIC GRAPHICNAME = "a4740084p" WIDTH = "6.903in" HEIGHT = "2.556in" />
</FIGURE>
</PARA>
</SECTION>
<SECTION SCID = "T010037A093S"><SCTITLE/>

<PARA INFOID = "T010054A093" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "20Sep2003"     INFOTYPE = "PARTS" INDSW = "ON">
<TITLE>Fuel Injector</TITLE>
<LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>A 12-hole ultra-fine atomization injector has been adopted. It is mounted directly to the cylinder head, shortening the distance to the combustion chamber and reducing fuel adhesion to the intake port, for excellent fuel economy and emission performance.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<FIGURE>
<GRAPHIC GRAPHICNAME = "a4740085p" WIDTH = "6.903in" HEIGHT = "3.153in" />
</FIGURE>
<SPEC ID = "T010054A093X01" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>Fuel Injector Specifications</TITLE>
<TABLE FRAME = "ALL" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1">
<TGROUP COLS = "2" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1" TGROUPSTYLE = "Table_01">
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "1" COLNAME = "1" COLWIDTH = "49%"/>
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "2" COLNAME = "2" COLWIDTH = "49%"/>
<TBODY>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>Injection Hole Diameter [mm]</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2" ALIGN = "CENTER"><PTXT>0.20</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "0">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>Number of Injection Holes</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2" ALIGN = "CENTER"><PTXT>12</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
</TBODY>
</TGROUP></TABLE></SPEC>
</PARA>
</SECTION>
<SECTION SCID = "T010037A409S"><SCTITLE/>

<PARA INFOID = "T010037A409" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "8Dec2003"     INFOTYPE = "PARTS" INDSW = "ON">
<TITLE>Charcoal Canister</TITLE>
<LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>Canister purge control, which draws fuel evaporative gas generated from the fuel tank into the intake port and burns it, has been adopted.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>Integrated with the fuel pump and located inside the fuel tank. This reduces the number of parts, making the fuel system lighter and more compact.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<FIGURE>
<GRAPHIC GRAPHICNAME = "a4740018p" WIDTH = "6.903in" HEIGHT = "2.792in" />
</FIGURE>
</PARA>
</SECTION>
<SECTION SCID = "T010037T038S"><SCTITLE/>

<PARA INFOID = "T010054T038" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "11Apr2005"     INFOTYPE = "PARTS" INDSW = "ON">
<TITLE>VSV for Canister Purge</TITLE>
<LIST1><ITEM><PTXT>The canister purge volume is controlled by the signal (duty signal) from the engine control computer. The purge volume is determined by the ratio of the ON and OFF times of the signal (duty ratio).</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>The piping of the canister purge VSV has been optimized to reduce evaporative pulsation noise.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<FIGURE>
<GRAPHIC GRAPHICNAME = "a4600019p" WIDTH = "6.903in" HEIGHT = "2.514in" />
</FIGURE>
</PARA>
</SECTION>
